<title>UK: ITALY'S AGIP TO LIFT IRAQ CRUDE LATE AUGUST - TRADE.</title>
<headline>ITALY'S AGIP TO LIFT IRAQ CRUDE LATE AUGUST - TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian state oil company Agip expects to lift one million barrels of Iraqi crude oil later this month under the terms of the U.N. oil-for-food deal, traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>Agip is awaiting final confirmation of its nomination from Iraq's State Oil Marketing Organisation (SOMO) but expects to lift one cargo of sour Kirkuk Blend from the Turkish port of Ceyhan in the second half of August, they said.</p>
<p>The company lifted 10,000 bpd of Kirkuk in the first 180-day period of the U.N. programme which allows Baghdad to sell $2 billion every six months to raise money for food and medicines.</p>
<p>Exports in the second period, which began on June 5, will be squeezed into less than four months following Iraq's insistence on a revised aid distribution plan which was only approved last week.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
